 of Judah, and the sons of the brethren of Ahaziah, that ministered to Ahaziah, he slew them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ)And he sought Ahaziah: and they caught him, (for he was hid in Samaria,) and brought him to Jehu: and when they had slain him, they buried him: Because, said they, he is the son of Jehoshaphat, who sought the LORD with all his heart. So the house of Ahaziah had no power to keep still the kingdom.¦layout ªlast_verse	…¤book§chapter«first_verse
